@startuml
!theme plain

title P1 Self-Service Onboarding Flows

actor User
participant "Pulsar App" as App
participant "Secure Storage" as Store
participant "Coordinator API" as API
database "Identity Store" as DB
participant "Telegram Bot" as Bot

== Create Orbit ==
User -> App: Create Barycenter
App -> API: POST /v1/onboarding/orbits
API -> DB: create orbit + app actor + membership\n+ slot + node/control creds\n+ recovery hash + audit event
DB --> API: plaintext creds + recovery secret
API --> App: orbit info + node/control creds + recovery secret
App -> Store: persist creds in Keychain/DPAPI
App --> User: show recovery secret once

== Join by Device Invite ==
User -> App: Enter invite code / open deep link
App -> API: POST /v1/device-invites/consume
API -> DB: burn invite, add actor membership,\nallocate slot, mint creds, audit
DB --> API: plaintext node/control creds
API --> App: orbit info + creds
App -> Store: persist creds

== Recover Control Access ==
User -> App: Enter recovery secret
App -> API: POST recovery endpoint
API -> DB: verify recovery hash,\nreissue control credential,\naudit event
DB --> API: new control credential
API --> App: control credential only
App -> Store: replace control credential,\npreserve node credential state

== Link Telegram ==
User -> App: Request Telegram link code
App -> API: POST /v1/telegram-links
API -> DB: mint one-time bot link code
API --> App: bot link code
User -> Bot: send link code
Bot -> API: consume code with Telegram identity
API -> DB: join or merge Telegram actor\ninto existing membership policy
Bot --> User: link confirmation

note over API,DB
  Node tokens never authorize create, invite,
  upload, recovery, or Telegram-link actions.
  Pair compatibility stays additive and
  legacy slots keep their current tokens.
end note

@enduml
